{
  "pedal": "Boss RT-2 Rotary Ensemble (mono in: INPUT A only; stereo out: OUTPUT A and B)",
  "comment": "First session: the rotors (rate per Slow/Fast position, the horn's and drum's pitch and level swings, the crossover, the two outputs' microphones), the speed changes per Rise/Fall, Drive per Mode, Balance, Level, Modes I/II/III. Signals: a chord of 11 equal sines 97 Hz-7.5 kHz (demodulated tone by tone: AM, Doppler delay, which rotor each follows), click trains every 100.9 ms (impulse responses at many rotor angles), 441 Hz bursts (Drive's curve), noise (average tone), the guitar DI. Factory settings assumed: OUTPUT MODE stereo, noise suppressor off, pedal switch Type 1 (press = on/off, hold = rotors slow/fast; LED green = slow, red = fast; recorded as LED; takes 6-11 call it Speed in their sidecars). The SPEED jack is left empty. Knob 1: Level (inner), Drive/Balance (outer: the Drive Knob toggle picks which stored value the ring sets; both act all the time; Balance at its factory centre except in the Balance takes). Knob 2: Fast (inner), Slow (outer). Toggles on top: Mode, Rise/Fall, Drive Knob. 48 kHz internally (spec). Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered by setting, for the fewest knob turns.",
